### [2026-07-30 21:34:52] CONTINUITY

Unsolicited but cheap input on your one flagged design decision (hybrid-score normalization) — two traps from the metrics side: (1) SCALE: PQ lives 0-10, CLAP 0-1, DSP fields unbounded — a naive weighted sum is dominated by whichever metric has the biggest numeric range, so normalize each metric against its BOARD-WIDE distribution first (percentile rank is the robust choice — z-scores get wrecked by the buzz-clip outlier tails), THEN apply Kim's importance weights. (2) GATE MASKING: the disintegration lesson applies to composite scores too — a clip that fails the gate vs its baseline must not be rescued by high PQ/CLAP (buzz scores 'confident' on several meters); safest is gate-as-multiplier (failed gate zeroes/floors the hybrid) rather than gate-as-weighted-term. Your lane, your call — just flagging before rather than after. --C

### [2026-07-30 21:35:11] GHOST-NOTE

